{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And so. The commentators have erred in this verse. One interprets קברים as קבורים (buried), שמורים as kept in their palace, ובאו as ויבואו (and they came), ויהלכו as doing their will, וישתכחו as the Targum's וימצאו (and were found). Others said that ובאו means נעלמו (disappeared), like ובא השמש (and the sun came = set). This too is not correct, for this meaning is found only with the sun, because it is the opposite of יצא (went forth); and so it says, השמש יצא על הארץ. And commentators said בא בשכרו is like it, but it is not so; rather, בא לו — this thing did not come to him, that he should not be paid his wage. And likewise many paytanim erred, saying מאורה and completing the verse קומי אורי כי בא אורך, and their words contradict each other if they do not complete the verse, and this is its meaning: כי נעלם אורך הקדמון וזרח עליך כבוד ה׳. And so he will interpret לא יהיה לך עוד השמש לאור יומם. And this is the meaning of the verse: ובכן, like the Targum of אז. And the matter: when I set my heart, then I saw the wicked who ruled over men and did them evil — they died without suffering, buried in their grave, as the matter of כי אין חרצובות למותם. And they came into the world a second time; the meaning is that their sons come and stand in their place, and their memory endures. And אשר ממקום קדוש יהלכו: the meaning is that the holy ones who die without a son are forgotten in the city where they were — והם אשר עשו כן האמת, like the daughters of Zelophehad. How is the memory of the righteous cut off and all the good he did forgotten, while the wicked dies in peace and leaves sons in his place? גם זה הבל."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The comment is textually dense and possibly corrupt in places (e.g., והם אשר עשו כן האמת); translated hyper-literally without smoothing. Resolved ה׳ as HaShem per divine-name rules. The repeated וכן / וזה פירוש transitions are ambiguous in their referents and left as rendered."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:35.058556356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}